        {
          "file": ".github/workflows/control.yml",
          "line": 10,
          "message": ".github/workflows/control.yml:10: job `verify` step 2 pins host port `8080` in `8080:80`. Hosted and shared runners collide when a publish mapping fixes the host port. Publish a Docker-allocated port (`127.0.0.1::5432`, `::5432`, `0:5432`, or the container port only). A variable host port is not judged.",
          "rule": "github-actions-docker-host-ports",
          "sourceLine": "- run: docker run --publish 8080:80 example-image",
          "target": "verify"
        },
        {
          "file": ".github/workflows/control.yml",
          "line": 11,
          "message": ".github/workflows/control.yml:11: job `verify` step 3 downloads `https://example.invalid/tool` with `curl` and does not verify the bytes in this step. An http(s) download can change between runs. Verify it here with `sha256sum -c` or `shasum -a 256 -c` against a downloaded checksum file, use a trusted host, or add `# integrity-check: skip reason=<slug>`.",
          "rule": "github-actions-download-integrity",
          "sourceLine": "- run: curl -fsSL https://example.invalid/tool -o example.sh",
          "target": "verify"
        },
        {
          "file": ".github/workflows/control.yml",
          "line": 13,
          "message": ".github/workflows/control.yml:13: job `verify` step 4 waits in a `until` loop that sleeps and runs `gh run view`. A job that polls another job or workflow burns runner minutes. Depend on the work with `needs`, or react to an event (`workflow_run`, `merge_group`) instead of polling.",
          "rule": "github-actions-no-poll-wait-job",
          "sourceLine": "until gh run view 123; do",
          "target": "verify"
        },
        {
          "file": ".github/workflows/control.yml",
          "line": 16,
          "message": ".github/workflows/control.yml:16: job `verify` step 5 diffs the pull request base SHA against the head SHA with a two-dot or two-argument range, which also lists base-branch changes made after the branch point, so path filters and changed-file checks run on the wrong set. Use a three-dot diff (`git diff <base>...<head>`) after fetching enough history, or `git diff HEAD^1 HEAD` on the merge commit.",
          "rule": "github-actions-pr-diff-range",
          "sourceLine": "- run: git diff --name-only \"${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}\" \"${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}\"",
          "target": "verify"
        },
        {
          "file": ".github/workflows/control.yml",
          "line": 17,
          "message": ".github/workflows/control.yml:17: job `verify` step 6 narrows Vitest project `example` with positional test file `src/item.test.ts`. Whole-project selection is required for this project. Run the configured project without a positional file argument.",
          "rule": "github-actions-vitest-project-selection",
          "sourceLine": "- run: pnpm exec vitest run --project example src/item.test.ts",
          "target": "src/item.test.ts"
        },
        {
          "file": ".github/workflows/control.yml",
          "line": 9,
          "message": ".github/workflows/control.yml: job \"verify\" step \"example/setup@aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\" uses a configured action and must set timeout-minutes: 2; got null",
          "rule": "github-actions-action-timeout-pair",
          "sourceLine": "- uses: example/setup@aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
          "target": "verify"
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    }
